    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37052" root="كعنب" body-key="k">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَعْنَبٌ</span></b>  <i>Short:</i> (K:) an epithet applied to a
man. (Az.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الكَعْنَبُ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الكُعَانِبُ</span> <i>The lion.</i>
(K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَعَانِبُ</span> <i>Knobs,</i> or <i>protuberances,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُجَرٌ</span>,)
of the head. (K.) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَعْنَبٌ</span> A man <i>having knobs,</i>
or <i>protuberances,</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُجَرٌ</span>,) <i>on his head.</i> (K.)

